WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.529 --> 00:00:08.550
I want to start with a question…

00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:11.590
What would you do if you had 250 TRILLION
dollars?

00:00:11.590 --> 00:00:14.950
I’m sure there are lots of things you would
like to do with that amount of money.

00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:18.890
But what if I told you that those 250 Trillion
dollars were from ZIMBABWE?

00:00:18.890 --> 00:00:24.640
Well, that’s a totally different question
because, in 2015, 250 trillion Zimbabwean

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:27.690
dollars were the equivalent of…

00:00:27.690 --> 00:00:28.690
ONE US DOLLAR!!!

00:00:28.690 --> 00:00:29.690
Yep.

00:00:29.690 --> 00:00:30.690
You heard that right.

00:00:30.690 --> 00:00:41.079
The truth is Zimbabwe is like Venezuela but…
at a massive scale.

00:00:41.079 --> 00:00:44.289
This country has suffered the worse hyperinflation
of all time.

00:00:44.289 --> 00:00:50.790
Since, more or less, the year 2000, prices
were rising higher and higher at a mind-boggling

00:00:50.790 --> 00:00:51.790
pace.

00:00:51.790 --> 00:00:55.359
In 2008, a piece of bread was worth 10,000
Zimbabwean dollars.

00:00:55.359 --> 00:00:57.010
And now you might wonder…

00:00:57.010 --> 00:00:58.140
How did this happen?

00:00:58.140 --> 00:00:59.960
Well… the answer is simple.

00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:02.409
One day, ROBERT MUGABE told his finance minister…

00:01:02.409 --> 00:01:07.140
‘Dude, I don’t care how you do it but
we need money’

00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:08.690
And what did the minister do?

00:01:08.690 --> 00:01:13.080
Well… he just pressed the money printing
button like there was no tomorrow.

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:17.390
So in conclusion: Zimbabwe had to get rid
of their own national currency and let their

00:01:17.390 --> 00:01:23.670
economy be dominated by foreign currencies,
especially the American dollar.

00:01:23.670 --> 00:01:26.310
But…

00:01:26.310 --> 00:01:30.990
What’s going on in ZIMBABWE now?

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:36.700
In the latest days of 2017, this country appeared
on the news because a coup d’etat spelled

00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:39.939
the end of Mugabe’s 37 year long dictatorship.

00:01:39.939 --> 00:01:44.659
And yes, my dear friends at VisualPolitik,
we must say that coup d’etats are not what

00:01:44.659 --> 00:01:45.710
they used to be.

00:01:45.710 --> 00:01:48.479
This was the DIET COKE version of a coup d’etat.

00:01:48.479 --> 00:01:52.640
Just look at this.

00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:58.299
Zimbabwe: Robert Mugabe to get $10m payoff
and immunity for his family.

00:01:58.299 --> 00:02:02.009
In fact, this has been more of a soap opera.

00:02:02.009 --> 00:02:06.990
Mugabe, at 93 years old, wanted to die in
power and he also wanted his wife, 52 years

00:02:06.990 --> 00:02:09.479
old, to inherit the presidency.

00:02:09.479 --> 00:02:13.710
You know, these kinds of things can only happen
in countries like Argentina, North Korea or…

00:02:13.710 --> 00:02:15.480
the Front National in France.

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:18.629
So as you can imagine, a lot of people did
not agree with this.

00:02:18.629 --> 00:02:22.909
So the Mugabe klan sent all their political
opponents out of the country.

00:02:22.909 --> 00:02:26.890
This is what happened at the beginning of
November 2017, when they kicked out the Vicepresident

00:02:26.890 --> 00:02:41.180
EMMERSON MNANGAWA.

00:02:41.180 --> 00:02:43.360
The army’s reaction was immediate.

00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:45.370
And you know the rest.

00:02:45.370 --> 00:02:48.319
But now the questions about Zimbabwe’s future
are many.

00:02:48.319 --> 00:02:50.069
Is MNANGAWA the new MUGABE?

00:02:50.069 --> 00:02:55.610
Can this man resurrect Zimbabwe’s economy?

00:02:55.610 --> 00:02:58.900
Today, we are going to answer these questions.

00:02:58.900 --> 00:03:04.840
But before we do, let’s take a look back
at history.

00:03:04.840 --> 00:03:07.599
TITLE: THE 2000 EFFECT

00:03:07.599 --> 00:03:10.689
Yes, you are right, Zimbabwe’s economy is
a total disaster.

00:03:10.689 --> 00:03:13.269
And I know what you are thinking.

00:03:13.269 --> 00:03:18.830
If you make a cocktail where you mix dictatorship
and Africa, what you get is corruption and

00:03:18.830 --> 00:03:20.480
poverty, right?

00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:24.330
Well… you are kind of right.

00:03:24.330 --> 00:03:25.780
But not as much as you might think.

00:03:25.780 --> 00:03:29.430
In fact, there was a time where Zimbabwe was
known as the African jewel.

00:03:29.430 --> 00:03:32.159
Their fertile soil allowed this country to
become the whole continent’s barn.

00:03:32.159 --> 00:03:33.890
And now you might wonder…

00:03:33.890 --> 00:03:37.810
What happened in a country with so many natural
resources, so many rich lands, so many gold

00:03:37.810 --> 00:03:40.900
mines, to make it become such a catastrophe?

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:44.810
Well… the answer has a name and a surname,
and that is ROBERT MUGABE.

00:03:44.810 --> 00:03:47.370
Zimbabwe has been an independent country for
37 years.

00:03:47.370 --> 00:03:50.990
And 37 years is the time Mugabe has been in
power.

00:03:50.990 --> 00:03:56.300
The decolonization process of the, so called,
SOUTH RHODESIA, a British colony, ended in

00:03:56.300 --> 00:03:58.900
a 15 year civil war.

00:03:58.900 --> 00:04:06.480
On one hand, we had the white minority, that
made up just 5% of the population.

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:10.230
Despite what you might think, they didn’t
have the support of the Western powers.

00:04:10.230 --> 00:04:13.989
They declared their independence unilaterally
and, therefore, any other country supported

00:04:13.989 --> 00:04:14.989
them.

00:04:14.989 --> 00:04:18.890
On the other hand, you had the guerrilla troops,
led by ROBERT MUGABE, a man who combined anti

00:04:18.890 --> 00:04:22.490
imperialist nationalism with a hardcore communist
view.

00:04:22.490 --> 00:04:25.699
Back then, Margaret THATCHER was the UK’s
Prime Minister.

00:04:25.699 --> 00:04:28.650
And you might think now… hmm, cold war,
plus, a

00:04:28.650 --> 00:04:30.350
communist leader, plus, Margaret Thatcher…

00:04:30.350 --> 00:04:36.440
this sounds like an explosive combination,
right?

00:04:36.440 --> 00:04:39.960
Well… you are wrong.

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:44.650
Back then, the UK’s priority was to let
their former colonies become healthy democracies.

00:04:44.650 --> 00:04:48.460
And this is why Thatcher herself signed a
peace agreement with the Zimbabwean guerrilla

00:04:48.460 --> 00:04:51.150
fighters and organized elections in the country.

00:04:51.150 --> 00:04:54.650
These elections were as fair as they could
be given that the country had just ended a

00:04:54.650 --> 00:04:57.330
civil war and had guerrilla warriors all over
the place.

00:04:57.330 --> 00:04:59.390
And… who won this election?

00:04:59.390 --> 00:05:00.390
Exactly!

00:05:00.390 --> 00:05:01.390
Robert Mugabe!

00:05:01.390 --> 00:05:02.390
And now you might wonder…

00:05:02.390 --> 00:05:04.419
did he cheat or was it a fair victory?

00:05:04.419 --> 00:05:09.800
Well…. the evidence suggests that he really
have the support.

00:05:09.800 --> 00:05:19.830
You see, among the majority of the black population
in Zimbabwe, there are 2 major ethnic groups.

00:05:19.830 --> 00:05:22.920
You have the SHONA, who make up 80% of the
population.

00:05:22.920 --> 00:05:25.289
And then you have the MATABELE, who are just
10%.

00:05:25.289 --> 00:05:26.289
Well…

00:05:26.289 --> 00:05:27.870
Robert Mugabe belongs to the SHONA group.

00:05:27.870 --> 00:05:31.130
And this is why it is no surprise that he
won with 60% of the vote.

00:05:31.130 --> 00:05:36.900
So in 1980, the UK granted independence to
Rhodesia, and this is how ZIMBABWE as a sovereign

00:05:36.900 --> 00:05:39.380
country, with Mugabe as the president, was
born.

00:05:39.380 --> 00:05:43.740
And during the first 7 years he grabbed all
the power.

00:05:43.740 --> 00:05:51.430
And in terms of the economy, we must admit
things worked… in the beginning.

00:05:51.430 --> 00:05:57.660
Mugabe respected the property rights of the
white population.

00:05:57.660 --> 00:06:02.460
But, in a very Venezuelan fashion, he sent
all the savings from the colonial times.

00:06:02.460 --> 00:06:06.240
And, well… we have to admit that although
it didn’t work in the long run, Mugabe achieved

00:06:06.240 --> 00:06:07.240
a great goal.

00:06:07.240 --> 00:06:10.900
Under his rule, Zimbabwe achieved the highest
literacy rate in Africa.

00:06:10.900 --> 00:06:13.240
90% of Zimbabweans can read and write.

00:06:13.240 --> 00:06:17.080
And what’s the next thing on the to-do list
for a dictator?

00:06:17.080 --> 00:06:19.310
Well… get rid of the opposition!

00:06:19.310 --> 00:06:22.099
In this chapter, Mugabe didn’t save a penny.

00:06:22.099 --> 00:06:26.630
He sent the 5th garrison of his army to North
Korea so they could learn state of the art

00:06:26.630 --> 00:06:33.610
methods for oppression.

00:06:33.610 --> 00:06:38.069
And then, when those soldiers came back, he
said… ‘hey guys, now go to the MATABELES

00:06:38.069 --> 00:06:39.069
and… wipe them out!!!!’.

00:06:39.069 --> 00:06:41.110
This is how the GURUKAHUNDI started.

00:06:41.110 --> 00:06:44.990
GURUKAHUNDI means, in the SHONA language,
‘early rain that cleans the straws by the

00:06:44.990 --> 00:06:47.229
inside before the spring rains come’.

00:06:47.229 --> 00:06:49.240
Yeah, SHONAS are pretty poetic.

00:06:49.240 --> 00:06:53.620
But, despite the beautiful name, GURUKAHUNDI
was an ethic cleansing to the manual.

00:06:53.620 --> 00:07:00.069
More than 20,000 people died.

00:07:00.069 --> 00:07:04.490
But Mugabe gained great stability.

00:07:04.490 --> 00:07:07.509
All his political foes had been killed.

00:07:07.509 --> 00:07:10.190
But in the year 2000, things changed.

00:07:10.190 --> 00:07:15.190
That year, Mugabe decided to start an agricultural
revolution, Mao style.

00:07:15.190 --> 00:07:18.210
It was a real revolution.

00:07:18.210 --> 00:07:20.389
Everything changed… for worse.

00:07:20.389 --> 00:07:24.120
Mugabe decided that the best lands couldn’t
be owned by the White minority.

00:07:24.120 --> 00:07:28.280
So he expropriated those and gave to… surprise!

00:07:28.280 --> 00:07:29.280
Surprise!

00:07:29.280 --> 00:07:31.150
His ministers and political allies!

00:07:31.150 --> 00:07:34.700
He gave them the land but not the knowledge
to tend to it.

00:07:34.700 --> 00:07:39.220
So… production fell sharply while hyperinflation
destroyed the rest of the industries.

00:07:39.220 --> 00:07:44.310
Since then, Zimbabwe has been a living hell.

00:07:44.310 --> 00:07:48.039
THE TIME OF THE CROCODILE

00:07:48.039 --> 00:07:51.889
They say crocodiles wait beneath the water,
showing just their eyes and their nostrils

00:07:51.889 --> 00:07:53.190
until a victim appears.

00:07:53.190 --> 00:07:55.910
Then, they open their jaws and eat them.

00:07:55.910 --> 00:08:01.539
This is why the new president of Zimbabwe,
Emerson Mnangagwa is known as ‘THE CROCODILE’

00:08:01.539 --> 00:08:04.670
MNANGAGWA was one of those guerrilla leaders
during the civil war.

00:08:04.670 --> 00:08:07.389
And he has been a minister since 1980.

00:08:07.389 --> 00:08:11.180
So he spent all his life waiting under the
shadow of the dictator.

00:08:11.180 --> 00:08:13.270
But his moment has come.

00:08:13.270 --> 00:08:16.599
So far, after this coup d’etat, his first
steps haven’t been very risky.

00:08:16.599 --> 00:08:20.460
Here is an example.

00:08:20.460 --> 00:08:25.520
Zimbabwe leader's Cabinet heavy on military,
ruling party

00:08:25.520 --> 00:08:28.280
But this is not enough for Zimbabwe and he
still has a lot of work ahead.

00:08:28.280 --> 00:08:32.390
This is one of the biggest steps he has already
taken.

00:08:32.390 --> 00:08:36.300
Govt amends Indigenisation Law

00:08:36.300 --> 00:08:40.340
The Indigenisation Law is another economic
policy made by Mugabe.

00:08:40.340 --> 00:08:44.160
In this case, he said bigger companies couldn’t
belong to white people.

00:08:44.160 --> 00:08:48.320
As you can imagine, the white minority that
used to live in the country has already emigrated.

00:08:48.320 --> 00:08:49.840
They used to be a 5% of the population.

00:08:49.840 --> 00:08:51.910
Now they are just 1%.

00:08:51.910 --> 00:08:54.640
But now the CROCODILE wants foreign investment.

00:08:54.640 --> 00:09:03.160
And rejecting someone because of his or her
race doesn’t seem like a good economic idea.

00:09:03.160 --> 00:09:07.570
But wait a minute because… despite all of
that, this new president of Zimbabwe might

00:09:07.570 --> 00:09:09.300
not be the right man for the job!

00:09:09.300 --> 00:09:12.030
Look, in a country like this, it’s very
easy to find dark spots in the curriculum

00:09:12.030 --> 00:09:15.280
of a politician who’s served such a crazy
dictator.

00:09:15.280 --> 00:09:19.740
And… guess what the CROCODILE did in the
80s!

00:09:19.740 --> 00:09:24.380
Yes, he was the minister of…

00:09:24.380 --> 00:09:25.380
NATIONAL SECURITY!

00:09:25.380 --> 00:09:28.390
So… he would have had something to do with
the GURUKAHUNDI genocide.

00:09:28.390 --> 00:09:33.220
And, as you can imagine, being a genocide
executor doesn’t seem like the best introduction

00:09:33.220 --> 00:09:35.170
letter to lead a country, right?

00:09:35.170 --> 00:09:36.180
So now you might wonder…

00:09:36.180 --> 00:09:38.160
Is there any other person for this job?

00:09:38.160 --> 00:09:42.820
Someone who can really become the opposition
to the regime?

00:09:42.820 --> 00:09:43.820
The answer is YES.

00:09:43.820 --> 00:09:46.820
In 2008, there was a political party called
MOVEMENT FOR A DEMOCRATIC CHANGE.

00:09:46.820 --> 00:09:49.790
And, surprisingly, they beat Mugabe in those
elections.

00:09:49.790 --> 00:09:50.790
Yep.

00:09:50.790 --> 00:09:51.790
You heard that right.

00:09:51.790 --> 00:09:56.470
In a dictatorship like Zimbabwe, this meant
a big time political crisis.

00:09:56.470 --> 00:10:05.580
He couldn’t destroy an opponent with such
a huge amount of political capital.

00:10:05.580 --> 00:10:08.110
But he couldn’t let him win either.

00:10:08.110 --> 00:10:10.510
And, finally, Mugabe came up with a solomonic
decision.

00:10:10.510 --> 00:10:12.380
He would remain the president, but he would
let

00:10:12.380 --> 00:10:15.400
his opponent, MORGAN TSVANGIRAI, become the
Prime Minister.

00:10:15.400 --> 00:10:18.070
Of course, this Prime Minister remained in
power for just 4 years.

00:10:18.070 --> 00:10:23.310
It was during those 4 years that Zimbabwe
started using USD as an official currency

00:10:23.310 --> 00:10:25.170
after the collapse of their local one.

00:10:25.170 --> 00:10:30.840
But the country remained in dire straits.

00:10:30.840 --> 00:10:35.390
Zimbabwe’s unemployment rate at 90 percent

00:10:35.390 --> 00:10:38.340
This is why, Tsvangirai has lost a lot of
political capital.

00:10:38.340 --> 00:10:43.260
So… it seems that in the next election,
the CROCODILE has all the chances to win.

00:10:43.260 --> 00:10:45.520
Besides, the army is going to control the
process.

00:10:45.520 --> 00:10:47.730
And the army supports the Crocodile.

00:10:47.730 --> 00:10:49.170
One thing must be said here.

00:10:49.170 --> 00:10:53.080
Whoever leads the country next will have a
great advantage…

00:10:53.080 --> 00:11:02.980
it is impossible to do any worse than their
predecessor.

00:11:02.980 --> 00:11:03.980
So now the question is…

00:11:03.980 --> 00:11:09.640
Do you think this CROCODILE will be able to
take Zimbabwe back to the African jewel times?

00:11:09.640 --> 00:11:12.410
Or he will do the same as Mugabe did?

00:11:12.410 --> 00:11:15.320
